    "/* The name a card's row does not print travels on the connector instead, and it has to stay legible on\n   top of the dotted backdrop, so it gets the panel's own fill behind it rather than a heavier line. It is\n   a second reading of the same information as the row it points at, so it is allowed to be quieter than\n   the text — but not quieter than the backdrop's own noise, which is what the halo is for. */",
    "/* Without this the chip is an inline box, `width` is ignored and the colour never paints — measured in\n     a browser, where the swatch came out 1px wide. `inline-block` keeps it inside the value's text run so\n     an ellipsized value still carries its colour with it. */",
