    "/* #e36209 measured 2.51:1 on a hovered key's wash and 3.04:1 on a white card — the JSON faces paint\n     their keys, and every code block its `.token.property` and `.token.deleted`, with this token, so it\n     carries text, not decoration. #8d4500 is the same hue at the depth that clears 4.5:1 on all twelve\n     light backgrounds; the dark theme's #f69d50 already measured 4.72:1 and is untouched. */",
    "/* ── The stacking scale ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n     One named band per tier two overlapping surfaces actually compare on. Every number the app\n     paints today has a name here: nothing outside this list may write a `z-index` of its own.\n     `src/client/lib/z-index.ts` mirrors these values for surfaces whose stack level is set from JS,\n     and `tests/shared-component-contract.test.ts` pins the two against each other, so a band cannot\n     be added on one side only and no band may be re-tuned out of order.\n     The scale is strictly increasing. Below `--z-drawer` the numbers are counters inside one\n     surface's own stacking context — a slide stage, a kanban column, a prose widget — so they read\n     small and never meet the viewport-fixed tiers above them.\n     Two of these bands are named twice over, and both are debt with a pending rename rather than a\n     second tier: `--z-pop` (260) is the floating-menu tier `Z_INDEX.menu` calls \"menu\", and\n     `--z-pinned` (280) is what `Z_INDEX.hoverPinned` calls the pinned-card tier. The scale keeps the\n     CSS spelling; the JS keys change with their call sites. ─────────────────────────────────── */",
    "/* The projector's stage counter: beats a slide's own stacking context, never its controls. */",
    "/* A menu or popover drawn inside one surface's own context — the kanban board's column, filter,\n     sort, shortcuts and view-options panels, which only have to beat the board they sit in. */",
    "/* A handle floating over the text it belongs to (the block dragger). */",
    "/* A panel anchored to a control inside a reading or presentation surface. The widest-used band. */",
    "/* The drawer rail: above the app shell, below every dialog. */",
    "/* The settings panel — the first full-viewport dialog, so it opens under the rest. */",
    "/* The graph panel, which the settings panel must not cover. */",
    "/* A prompt or sheet a reader types into or picks from: the command palette, the omnisearch\n     prompt, a mobile filter sheet, an article or template preview, a graph overlay. */",
    "/* `Dialog`. The projector owns the viewport at this tier, and the rows it opens ride above it. */",
    "/* A picker that has to beat the dialog it was opened from (the emoji picker). */",
    "/* The floating `Menu` tier, and the image lightbox. `Z_INDEX.menu` names this band \"menu\". */",
    "/* A submenu flyout: one above the menu that opened it. */",
    "/* A wiki-link hover card, and a context menu opened over one. */",
    "/* A pinned hover card and the menus it owns. `Z_INDEX.hoverPinned` names this band. */",
    "/* A menu opened from a pinned card. The shelf's full-viewport drop veil rides this tier. */",
